  <media:group>
   <media:title>Masterclass with Pathé | Episode 6</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/sDs9LhX0zS0?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/sDs9LhX0zS0/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>How do you bring a story to life through images?
In this new masterclass, Cléa Cervellera, a master’s student at École Louis-Lumière, talks with cinematographer Nicolas Bolduc.
Aboard the #Peugeot5008, he shares his perspective on his profession and the creative choices that shape a film’s visual identity: lighting, framing and camera movements.
Blending artistic vision with technical expertise, this conversation explores the behind-the-scenes world of a profession that is essential to filmmaking, where every decision helps create an atmosphere and tell a story.

Because in cinema, images don’t just show a story. They tell it.

#Peugeot #PathéCinémas #Cinema #Masterclass #Cinematography #Pathé</media:description>
